{"line":55,"at":"2026-10-11T08:26:06.949Z","kind":"assistant","text":"The three clip edits on Seq are done, but the new scene above Scene 1 is not: Ghostnote can only add scenes at the end of the Launcher.\n\n- **Scene 2 → Scene 6:** moved.\n- **Scene 3:** deleted.\n- **Scene 1 → Scene 3:** copied. The host only copies one row down, so I copied via Scene 2 and then deleted that intermediate copy; Scene 2 is empty again.\n\nSeq now has clips in Scenes 1, 3, 4 and 6. I took \"Scene N\" to mean Launcher row N, since Ghostnote doesn't expose scene names.\n\nFor the new scene, the quickest route is to insert it yourself in Bitwig. The alternative is that I add a scene at the end and shift every clip on every track down one row. That leaves row 1 empty, but scene names and colours would stay where they are, so they would no longer line up with their clips. Say if you want that."}
